  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Start Fund III (GSF III) &#x2013; FCDO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OUTPUT 1: Quality and timely crisis alerts are raised, which align with the Start Fund niche. Fund decision-making is collaborative and informed by humanitarian expertise and local knowledge.OUTPUT 2: The network access learning, resources and training. Best-practice and innovation are made available and disseminated across network and sector.OUTPUT 3: The network access funds for humanitarian action, with local actors increasingly engaging with and gaining an increased proportion. Assurance and accountability measures are appropriate and implemented.OUTCOME 1: Humanitarian action is timely, data-driven, informed by affected populations, and reaching people in greatest need. When possible, populations are protected and assisted ahead of crisis onset.OUTCOME 2: Learning and feedback inform programming, leading to humanitarian action that is appropriate, efficient and effective.OUTCOME 3: Fund decision-making is participatory, inclusive and collaborative, and increasingly locally led.IMPACT: Crisis affected and at-risk populations are rapidly protected and assisted, mitigating harm and enabling early recovery. As a result, lives are saved, dignity is maintained, and resilience is built.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Start Fund III (GSF III) is funded by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) and managed by Start Network. The Start Fund is a multi-donor humanitarian funding mechanism that enables rapid, localised humanitarian response to neglected and under-the-radar crises globally. The fund supports anticipatory and rapid-onset responses, with a focus on increasing local leadership, data-driven decision-making, and community participation in humanitarian action. This third phase runs from October 2022 to March 2026.</narrative>
  </description>
